{
  "$comment": "TDSP 2.0 draft control-state test vectors (draft revision 5): each vector's operations, merged in any order and as a snapshot, give each member the right listed, on the document and on the layer — `read`, `write`, `revoked` (refused as `read` is, CTL-13, on every layer, LAY-5) or `unknown` (never named, refused by nothing after the bootstrap). On a member's target revoked is narrower than read than write; on a layer's, read than inherit (null) than write (CTL-23). Operations of different devices that name none of the others in `seen` are concurrent (CTL-22). Checked in src/test-vectors.test.ts.",
